# Karpathy guidelines

1. Think before coding — state assumptions; surface tradeoffs; ask when unclear.
2. Simplicity first — no speculative features/abstractions/config.
3. Surgical changes — touch only what the task needs.
4. Goal-driven execution — every step has a verify check; prefer red→green.
